    "updated_at": "2019-04-11T09:46:41Z",
    "body": "I think applying the `preventScroll` option only when the focus moves seems reasonable.\r\nWhen I first brought up this topic, I had assumed that focus moves around the page.\r\n\r\nFYI, [this demo](https://jihyerish.github.io/demos/all-about-focus/focus_api.html) shows how `focus()` works if the focus actually moves or not.\r\n(clicking the \"Redundant Focus\" button triggers `focus({preventScroll: true})` and then `focus({preventScroll: false})`)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/482045290/reactions",
