    "created_at": "2026-11-18T08:20:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T08:20:32Z",
    "body": "Following up on this, it looks spec might need some change to match browsers' behavior. Coming back to the default case where you only use `focus()` as @zcorpan asked before.\n\nThe following test case shows magenta in all engines except Servo (which follows the spec):\n```\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<style>\n* {\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  background: magenta;\n}\n#target {\n  margin-top: 200vh;\n  height: 100vh;\n  background: cyan;\n}\n#target:focus-visible {\n  outline: none;\n}\n</style>\n<div id=\"target\" tabindex=\"1\"></div>\n<script>\n  target.focus();\n  window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n    window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n      window.scrollTo(0,0);\n      target.focus();\n    });\n  });\n</script>\n```\n\nYou can test it live at https://people.igalia.com/mrego/html/focus-scroll-issue.html\n\nThe spec says:\n- The [`focus()` method steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#dom-focus) run the [focusing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focusing-steps) in step 2.\n- Step 5 of the focusing steps returns early when \"new focus target is the currently focused area of a top-level traversable\", but that only exits the focusing steps.\n- `focus()` then continues to [step 4](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#dom-focusoptions-preventscroll), which scrolls the element into view, because [`preventScroll`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#dom-focusoptions-preventscroll) defaults to false.\n\nThis might need a spec change, so the last point doesn't happen when focus hasn't changed. That's probably the way to go, given that many pages often call `focus()` on the already focused element, so following the current spec has performance implications.\n\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
